      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2011 The Authors; Internal Medicine Journal © 2011 Royal Australasian College of Physicians.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "Chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting remain among the most feared adverse effects for cancer patients."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "AIM",
            "content": "The aim of this study was to evaluate the efficacy and safety of a combination of aprepitant, palonosetron and dexamethasone as antiemetic prophylaxis in patients receiving multiple-day cisplatin-based chemotherapy."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "Forty-one solid cancer patients received aprepitant, palonosetron and dexamethasone during a 3-day cisplatin-based chemotherapy. Primary end-point was complete response in the overall phase (day 1 until 5 days after the end of chemotherapy)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Aprepitant in combination with palonosetron and dexamethasone was safe, with hiccups (31.7%), fatigue (17.1%), headache (14.6%) and constipation (12.2%) the most common treatment-related adverse events, mostly mild. Complete response was seen in 58.5% of patients in the overall phase. In 23 patients receiving aprepitant in combination with palonosetron and dexamethasone more than one cycle (range: 2-5 cycles), the cumulative emetic protection rate after five cycles was 0.82."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "This study shows aprepitant in combination with palonosetron and dexamethasone is safe and effectively controls chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting in patients undergoing 3-day cisplatin-based chemotherapy, moreover, the efficacy is maintained during multiple cycles."
          }
        ]
      },
